{"id": "EUVD-2026-93332", "enisaUuid": "5572ed02-947e-32ea-afe7-b83eb020a00a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nIB/IPoIB: Avoid restoring OPER_UP after multicast flush\n\nipoib_ib_dev_flush_light() temporarily clears IPOIB_FLAG_OPER_UP to\nprevent multicast joins while ipoib_mcast_dev_flush() is running, and\nrestores the flag afterwards if it was previously set.\n\nThis restore races with ipoib_ib_dev_down(). If the interface is brought\ndown while the flush is in progress, ipoib_ib_dev_down() clears\nIPOIB_FLAG_OPER_UP, but the flush path may set it again after the device\nhas already gone down.\n\nSince commit 894021a75291 (\"IB/ipoib: Make the carrier_on_task race\naware\"), ipoib_mcast_carrier_on_task() relies on IPOIB_FLAG_OPER_UP\nbeing cleared to terminate its rtnl_trylock() retry loop. If the flag is\nleft set after shutdown, the workqueue retries forever, causing teardown\nto deadlock when ipoib_ndo_uninit() waits in destroy_workqueue() while\nholding RTNL.\n\nInstead of overloading IPOIB_FLAG_OPER_UP to block multicast joins\nduring a light flush, introduce a dedicated IPOIB_FLAG_MCAST_FLUSH flag.\nUse it together with IPOIB_FLAG_OPER_UP to determine whether multicast\njoins are allowed, avoiding the race with device shutdown.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:46:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f973769fb7cb33ba0d4a64b7dcfee0cabaead938", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b72f38929f4b5aa83161fd3b22a7327207e51ec5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1b11e4b55b41d9e69a8e8d07622614202e2eaca9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/326f7d34bd7e64de535566b65c0533b640df5a81", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ad925d45f28464a5e043c9620880bb6a030da89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/188b334a6db36a8e0bfaaf59bc4020639a0f3aad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ff3add37c329704ec46181b4ae4f00f9f16ce6f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a141d3dc869d18b2eab35e999f4790a9b84e40f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8j4r-887v-cjjx", "CVE-2026-98347"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06fe45d4-ed43-3292-8f65-0adf2c808879", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "344bacca8cd811809fc33a249f2738ab757d327f <188b334a6db36a8e0bfaaf59bc4020639a0f3aad"}, {"id": "08286f2d-394a-311d-8b94-f97c6223c672", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.8"}, {"id": "127287ec-7c85-3d89-a202-dad3c7e50460", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "1ed5e61e-2aed-31f2-bb12-1bd2863f8336", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "231e9696-684d-3e3c-937d-00f29a35ce9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.16.39 <3.17"}, {"id": "318d16dc-8794-346b-a834-f77aeaff7b8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "3db0a487-ec4f-36d5-9e2f-77df64506ea6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "344bacca8cd811809fc33a249f2738ab757d327f <f973769fb7cb33ba0d4a64b7dcfee0cabaead938"}, {"id": "4915c333-9902-3513-897f-8bdd3ea78ba6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dfe809702a11bd7fb91c882fb55620e39ce22109"}, {"id": "4e128956-d75a-3539-bac8-83269878e6a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.2.84 <3.3"}, {"id": "4ecc5856-6854-3300-ab63-109709066624", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.7.7 <4.8"}, {"id": "5a11604c-77a0-35f3-b249-990e78613839", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "5ae978e3-9a6b-38a2-a22b-af44abab4e77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patc